"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a02c4e0b97326fb7276fd9c7481db631562fe3de96c382f9ceae62f2b38900a2","event_uuid":"a993ab40-98ce-4da7-9ccb-631cdead131d","position":{"commit_sha":null,"position":"1793760547181678311-a993ab40-98ce-4da7-9ccb-631cdead131d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1bf82c23e8512cbfb8fafd74b6b4d4f49c37330b15fcc6d00c7ac671d2588fe9","event_uuid":"f07d2f27-191e-4bd7-9091-1b10efb7ed38","position":{"commit_sha":null,"position":"1793763291917454423-f07d2f27-191e-4bd7-9091-1b10efb7ed38"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1023088d9904884bb1cddbc29114f2a899f1edb8cd3c4e125027f6fde0b4f9f9","event_uuid":"41d11950-b0c9-4585-9209-29e851692523","position":{"commit_sha":null,"position":"1793822680739388854-41d11950-b0c9-4585-9209-29e851692523"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ef50f1fdd001993e50a0cd9567cd4ce19d9e7a34095a1603ae5afc661a4475f4","event_uuid":"4aebca89-a9e1-4107-8250-c9d26b5fd427","position":{"commit_sha":null,"position":"1793822688188176485-4aebca89-a9e1-4107-8250-c9d26b5fd427"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793760466971365145,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a993ab40-98ce-4da7-9ccb-631cdead131d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e508-ce6c-2e52-4adc"}],"description":"# Live prompt-eval CI job scores coverage 0.0 on every spec\n\n## The gap\n\n`.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml`'s `eval-live` job calls `ev.run_eval(pid, max_cases=cap)`\ndirectly (`:136`). It does **not** wrap the call in `rebar.llm.gate_source.gate_read_root`, and\nit does **not** set `REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED`.\n\nSince epic raze-vet-ditch landed the agent-op safeguard, every agentic filesystem tool call\nmade outside a gate session raises:\n\n> agentic filesystem tools was attempted OUTSIDE the repo-snapshot gate process (epic\n> raze-vet-ditch): a tool-using agent must run inside rebar.llm.gate_source.gate_read_root\n> (attested snapshot or explicit local), never against the server's mutable checkout.\n\n(`src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py:144-162`)\n\n`run_eval` treats a solver exception as an **UNSCORED case, not a crash**\n(`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:670-682`), so the job does not fail loudly. It records every case\nas a run error, computes `coverage = 0.0`, fails `coverage_ok`, and reports\n`epoch_pass = [false, false, false]`.\n\nThe job is `continue-on-error: true` (`:95`) and only emits\n`::warning::live eval regressions (advisory)`. So a **total** scoring failure is\nindistinguishable from an ordinary advisory regression, and the live eval corpus has not\nactually been scoring anything since the safeguard landed.\n\n## Reproduction (measured)\n\nFull dataset, no cap, worktree `impl-e508` at `origin/main` 0e7401446c58:\n\n```\npython -c \"from rebar.llm.evals import eval as ev; ev.run_eval('code-review-tests')\"\n→ passed=false  coverage=0.0  epoch_pass=[false,false,false]  elapsed=40.4s\n```\n\nAll **117** case-runs (39 cases x 3 epochs) carry the identical gate error in the JUnit\n`message=` attribute. 40 seconds for 117 agentic code reviews is itself the tell: no model\ncall was ever made.\n\nWrapping the same call in a local-mode gate session makes the run proceed and reach the model:\n\n```python\nhandle = gate_source.resolve_gate_handle(None, gate_source.SOURCE_LOCAL, root, fetch=False)\nwith gate_source.gate_read_root(handle):\n    res = ev.run_eval(\"code-review-tests\", repo_root=root)\n```\n\n## Why it matters\n\nAny AC of the form \"the eval spec scores at or above its recorded pass bar, reproducible from\nthe committed spec\" is currently **not reproducible from the committed CI path** — only from a\nhand-wrapped local run. Several closed stories carry exactly that AC shape.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The `eval-live` job's live step runs `run_eval` inside a gate session, choosing the\n      source mode explicitly rather than relying on the configured default. `REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED`\n      is NOT used — the override is an audited escape hatch, not the fix.\n- [ ] A regression test asserts that the eval entry point used by CI runs under a gate session:\n      with the safeguard active and no override set, the entry point completes with\n      `coverage > 0` against an injected offline `solve`, and the unwrapped call is shown to\n      produce run errors. The test must fail against the current workflow's call shape.\n- [ ] `run_eval` (or the CI entry point) distinguishes \"every case errored\" from \"cases scored\n      and failed\" — a 0.0-coverage epoch is reported as a RUN FAILURE, not an advisory\n      regression, so this class of total failure cannot be silent again.\n- [ ] The portability constraint holds: the gate-session requirement is enforced in-process,\n      not by a GitHub-Actions-only step, so a project on another CI provider or no CI provider\n      gets the same behaviour.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["evals","ci"],"ticket_id":"77b6-868f-f4bd-461f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live prompt-eval CI job scores coverage 0.0 on every spec — run_eval is called outside a gate session","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5cdd6767-820e-4c31-91db-19557570237c","a993ab40-98ce-4da7-9ccb-631cdead131d","f07d2f27-191e-4bd7-9091-1b10efb7ed38","41d11950-b0c9-4585-9209-29e851692523","4aebca89-a9e1-4107-8250-c9d26b5fd427"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793822688188176486,"uuid":"129a147b-7260-4b07-ab54-3b1d598c6dcb"}